      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sound and Pitch\nA sound is a small change of air\npressure that travels as a wave. A\nmicrophone at one point in the air\nturns the wave into a signal p(t).\nThis part treats one note as that\nsignal. It explains what the\nsignal is made of, and which part\nof it the listener hears as the\npitch.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 22.5,
      "containerId": "node-baa14b68e522",
      "originalText": "Sound and Pitch\nA sound is a small change of air pressure that travels as a wave. A microphone at one point in the air turns the wave into a signal p(t). This part treats one note as that signal. It explains what the signal is made of, and which part of it the listener hears as the pitch.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "sound-and-pitch"
      }
    },
