    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2900043828,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-eeb9f88010d2",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1312.0,
      "y": 1160.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 227.5,
      "seed": 354216,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Octave\nAn octave is the interval between a pitch and\nthe pitch with twice its frequency. A4 is 440\nHz, A5 is 880 Hz and A3 is 220 Hz ([Octave](ht\ntps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octave)). The\noctave is also the step from the first\nharmonic to the second. Western notation gives\nnotes an octave apart the same letter name.\nMusic theory calls all pitches with one name,\nin every octave, a pitch class. The pitch\nclass C holds C1, C2, C3 and every other C\n([Pitch class](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P\nitch_class)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-eeb9f88010d2",
      "originalText": "Octave\nAn octave is the interval between a pitch and the pitch with twice its frequency. A4 is 440 Hz, A5 is 880 Hz and A3 is 220 Hz ([Octave](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octave)). The octave is also the step from the first harmonic to the second. Western notation gives notes an octave apart the same letter name. Music theory calls all pitches with one name, in every octave, a pitch class. The pitch class C holds C1, C2, C3 and every other C ([Pitch class](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitch_class)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "octave"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6924004571,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-f34b3615a862",
