    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1678662124,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-2ea2c5bd1795",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 726.0,
      "y": 2462.9411764705883,
      "strokeColor": "#0F172A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 377.99999999999994,
      "height": 225.0,
      "seed": 353669,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Piano Keyboard\nA modern piano has 88 keys: 52\nwhite keys and 36 black keys ([Pia\nno](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/\nPiano)). The lowest note is at the\nleft. Each key is one semitone\nabove its left neighbor, whatever\nits color ([Musical keyboard](http\ns://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musical_\nkeyboard)).",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 22.5,
      "containerId": "node-2ea2c5bd1795",
      "originalText": "The Piano Keyboard\nA modern piano has 88 keys: 52 white keys and 36 black keys ([Piano](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piano)). The lowest note is at the left. Each key is one semitone above its left neighbor, whatever its color ([Musical keyboard](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musical_keyboard)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "piano-keyboard"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
