    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9913574613,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-df463387ae15",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1312.0,
      "y": 3800.8057983467197,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 787.5,
      "seed": 754614,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Beat, Bar and Tempo\nPlayers count time in beats. The time\nsignature, two stacked numbers after the clef,\nsets the beat and groups the beats into bars,\nwhich are also called measures. The lower\nnumber names the note value that gets one\nbeat: 2 is a half note, 4 a quarter note and 8\nan eighth note. The upper number is the count\nof beats in one bar. In 4/4 time, one bar\nholds four quarter notes. The most common time\nsignatures are 2/4, 3/4 and 4/4 ([Time signatu\nre](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_signatu\nre)). Vertical bar lines separate the bars ([B\nar](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_%28music\n%29)).\n\nThe tempo is the speed of the beat in beats\nper minute (BPM). A metronome mark such as \u2669 =\n120 asks for 120 quarter notes per minute.\nMany scores use an Italian word instead of a\nnumber, or with it. The words give only rough\nspeeds, and the ranges below are for 4/4 time \n([Tempo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tempo))\n:\n\n- Largo: slow and broad, about 40 to 66 BPM.\n- Andante: at a walking pace, about 56 to 108\nBPM.\n- Allegro: fast and bright, about 120 to 156\nBPM.\n- Presto: very fast, about 168 to 200 BPM.\n\nA note of b beats lasts b \u00d7 60 / BPM seconds.\nAt \u2669 = 120, one beat lasts 60 / 120 = 0.5 s:\n\n| Symbol | Beats in 4/4 time | Seconds at \u2669 =\n120 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Whole note or whole rest | 4 | 2.0 |\n| Half note or half rest | 2 | 1.0 |\n| Dotted quarter note | 1.5 | 0.75 |\n| Quarter note or quarter rest | 1 | 0.5 |\n| Eighth note or eighth rest | 0.5 | 0.25 |\n\nOne bar of 4/4 time at this tempo lasts 2.0 s.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-df463387ae15",
      "originalText": "Beat, Bar and Tempo\nPlayers count time in beats. The time signature, two stacked numbers after the clef, sets the beat and groups the beats into bars, which are also called measures. The lower number names the note value that gets one beat: 2 is a half note, 4 a quarter note and 8 an eighth note. The upper number is the count of beats in one bar. In 4/4 time, one bar holds four quarter notes. The most common time signatures are 2/4, 3/4 and 4/4 ([Time signature](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_signature)). Vertical bar lines separate the bars ([Bar](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_%28music%29)).\n\nThe tempo is the speed of the beat in beats per minute (BPM). A metronome mark such as \u2669 = 120 asks for 120 quarter notes per minute. Many scores use an Italian word instead of a number, or with it. The words give only rough speeds, and the ranges below are for 4/4 time ([Tempo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tempo)):\n\n- Largo: slow and broad, about 40 to 66 BPM.\n- Andante: at a walking pace, about 56 to 108 BPM.\n- Allegro: fast and bright, about 120 to 156 BPM.\n- Presto: very fast, about 168 to 200 BPM.\n\nA note of b beats lasts b \u00d7 60 / BPM seconds. At \u2669 = 120, one beat lasts 60 / 120 = 0.5 s:\n\n| Symbol | Beats in 4/4 time | Seconds at \u2669 = 120 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Whole note or whole rest | 4 | 2.0 |\n| Half note or half rest | 2 | 1.0 |\n| Dotted quarter note | 1.5 | 0.75 |\n| Quarter note or quarter rest | 1 | 0.5 |\n| Eighth note or eighth rest | 0.5 | 0.25 |\n\nOne bar of 4/4 time at this tempo lasts 2.0 s.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "beat-bar-tempo"
      }
    },
